Subject: Mark xmlCatalogEntry.children _Atomic for capability-safe concurrent reads
Policy-Class: P2-Package
Rationale: xmlCatalogEntry.children is written under xmlCatalogMutex but read without holding the lock during concurrent catalog traversals; under Fil-C a non-atomic pointer load risks tearing a capability and triggering a safety trap.
Upstream-Status: Pending
Fil-C-Origin-Commits: cede3de02b42

diff --git a/catalog.c b/catalog.c
--- a/catalog.c
+++ b/catalog.c
@@ -110,7 +110,7 @@
 struct _xmlCatalogEntry {
     struct _xmlCatalogEntry *next;
     struct _xmlCatalogEntry *parent;
-    struct _xmlCatalogEntry *children;
+    struct _xmlCatalogEntry *_Atomic children;
     xmlCatalogEntryType type;
     xmlChar *name;
     xmlChar *value;
